<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.AFRICAN OCT CONSUMER PRICE INDEX UP 9.1 PCT Y/Y.</title>
<headline>S.AFRICAN OCT CONSUMER PRICE INDEX UP 9.1 PCT Y/Y.</headline>
<dateline>PRETORIA 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Africa's all-items consumer price index rose 1.0 percent in October from September after rising 1.0 percent in September, the Central Statistical Service said.</p>
<p>The year-on-year rise was 9.1 percent versus September's 8.4 percent.</p>
<p>A Reuters consensus poll of economists forecast a 0.7 percent month-on-month increase and an 8.8 percent year-on-year rise.  </p>
<p>Pct changes:</p>
<p>			 Year/year			     Month/month</p>
<p>			 Oct '96    Sep '96  Oct '95  -  latest  prev</p>
<p>All items	    9.1	   8.4     6.3	   1.0     1.0</p>
<p>Lower income gp    9.4	   8.6     5.4	   1.0     1.1</p>
<p>Middle income gp   9.6	   9.0     6.3	   0.9     1.1</p>
<p>Higher income gp   8.8	   8.1     6.6	   0.9     0.9</p>
<p>Food only	   12.4	  10.4    -1.5	   2.1     1.9</p>
<p>Indices:</p>
<p>			 Oct '96   Sep '96   Oct '95</p>
<p>All items	    188.4     186.6     172.7  </p>
<p>Lower income gp    187.0     185.1     171.0 </p>
<p>Middle income gp   191.9     190.1     175.1</p>
<p>Higher income gp   187.8     186.1     172.6</p>
<p>Food only	    218.8     214.2     194.6</p>
<p>(Index base 1990 = 100)</p>
